                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e596" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Please
                                        Contact Christina Mayr for Adoption Details:</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">If Cerberus sounds
                                        like a good fit for your home or foster program, please
                                        explore the full adoption package, and contact <fo:inline color="rgb(51 , 122 , 183)"><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:christinaemayr@gmail.com" fox:alt-text="Christina Mayr">Christina
                                            Mayr</fo:basic-link><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:christinaemayr@gmail.com" fox:alt-text=" "><fo:inline font-style="italic"/></fo:basic-link></fo:inline>,
                                        the foster coordinator. She’ll follow up shortly to begin
                                        the conversation!</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                            </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                        </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                        <fo:block-container break-before="page" space-before="1em" page-break-before="always" id="unique_2" chfox:nd-id="Common-Housing-Questions"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                            <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="2em" line-height="1.1em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0" id="ariaid-title2"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H1"><fo:marker marker-class-name="chaptertitle-only"><fo:inline/> <!--content(text)--><fo:inline>Common Housing Questions</fo:inline></fo:marker><fo:marker marker-class-name="chaptertitle-no-prefix"><fo:inline/> 2 - <!--content(text)--><fo:inline>Common Housing Questions</fo:inline></fo:marker><fo:marker marker-class-name="chaptertitle"><fo:inline/> | 2 - <!--content(text)--><fo:inline>Common Housing Questions</fo:inline></fo:marker><fo:inline>Chapter 2. </fo:inline><fo:inline>Common Housing Questions</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                            <fo:block-container page-break-before="avoid" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"> This reference
                                    answers the most common questions about preparing your home for
                                    Cerberus. </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e646" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        Do I need a house with a yard to adopt Cerberus?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: Yes, Cerberus
                                        is best suited to houses with backyards to allow him to meet
                                        his daily activity needs. </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e658" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        How long can Cerberus be left alone?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: He should not
                                        be left alone for more than 4–5 hours without a break. </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e670" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        Does Cerberus need a crate?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: Yes. Cerberus
                                        can tolerate crates and occasionally sleep in crates with
                                        appropriate encouragement. A soft-sided crate or a quiet
                                        “safe area” can be used for short rest periods, but a gated
                                        room or playpen is often a better option. </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e682" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        Can Cerberus live with cats or other small pets?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: No, Cerberus is
                                        not compatible with cats and has a strong prey drive. Small
                                        pets must have fully secure enclosures and be closely
                                        supervised if they are in the same home. Cerberus will
                                        likely do well with a calm, balanced dog after slow, careful
                                        introductions. Success depends on the other dog’s
                                        temperament and the adopter’s ability to manage the process.
                                    </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e695" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        How do I introduce Cerberus to children?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: Cerberus does
                                        best in adult-only homes or with children over five years
                                        old. Always supervise interactions, teach children to
                                        respect Cerberus's space, and avoid hugging or rough play.
                                    </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e707" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        How should I handle visitors coming to my home?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: Cerberus can be
                                        protective of his space. Keep him leashed or behind a gate
                                        during arrivals and reward calm behavior as guests enter.
                                        Give him time to adjust at his own pace. </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                                    <fo:block-container id="d38e719" font-size="1.17em" font-weight="700" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" page-break-after="avoid"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H2">Q:
                                        Who can I reach out to for adoption or training details and
                                        questions?</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A: For training
                                        information, please contact <fo:inline color="rgb(51 , 122 , 183)"><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:puptentialtraining@gmail.com" fox:alt-text="Lydia Registar (AAS, CPDT-KA)">Lydia
                                            Registar (AAS,
                                            CPDT-KA)</fo:basic-link><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:puptentialtraining@gmail.com" fox:alt-text=" "><fo:inline font-style="italic"/></fo:basic-link></fo:inline>.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">For adoption
                                        questions, please contact <fo:inline color="rgb(51 , 122 , 183)"><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:christinaemayr@gmail.com" fox:alt-text="Christina Mayr">Christina
                                            Mayr</fo:basic-link><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:christinaemayr@gmail.com" fox:alt-text=" "><fo:inline font-style="italic"/></fo:basic-link></fo:inline>
                                        or <fo:inline color="rgb(51 , 122 , 183)"><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:rubyleonaraine@protonmail.com" fox:alt-text="Ruby Leonaraine">Ruby
                                            Leonaraine</fo:basic-link><fo:basic-link show-destination="new" indicate-destination="true" external-destination="mailto:rubyleonaraine@protonmail.com" fox:alt-text=" "><fo:inline font-style="italic"/></fo:basic-link></fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                            </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                        </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                        <fo:block-container break-before="page" space-before="1em" page-break-before="always" id="unique_3" chfox:nd-id="photo-repository.dita"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="Sect">
                            <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="2em" line-height="1.1em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0" id="ariaid-title3"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0" role="H1"><fo:marker marker-class-name="chaptertitle-only"><fo:inline/> <!--content(text)--><fo:inline>Photo Repository</fo:inline></fo:marker><fo:marker marker-class-name="chaptertitle-no-prefix"><fo:inline/> 3 - <!--content(text)--><fo:inline>Photo Repository</fo:inline></fo:marker><fo:marker marker-class-name="chaptertitle"><fo:inline/> | 3 - <!--content(text)--><fo:inline>Photo Repository</fo:inline></fo:marker><fo:inline>Chapter 3. </fo:inline><fo:inline>Photo Repository</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                            <fo:block-container page-break-before="avoid" space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">This photo repository contains pictures of Cerberus with his
                                    foster family and friends. Photos are accompanied with a short
                                    description.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
